      "side": 1,
      "message": "This feels mis-phrased.\n\nThe key point here is that *all* writes must go through *this* single map class instance.\n\nIt\u0027s legal for other (non cached) readers to exist, but this must be the only writer (and thus it can cache).\n\nBasically we should have locking on the map.\n\nA readonly non-caching map does not need locking.\nA readwrite non-caching map user should flock(map_fd, LOCK_SH).\nA readwrite caching map user should flock(map_fd, LOCK_EX).\n\nman 2 flock\n\nWe should thus change the existing C/java BpfMap class implementations to take the appropriate locks on the bpf map fd (though the java fd caching might make it hard to do right...).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 28,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 28,
        "endChar": 92
      },
      "revId": "091889b2118ee7df8c005199c54972e0a37b542b",
